{"name":"Nosferatu","hex":"#a9a8a8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Nosferatu","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vampire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Nosferatu"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nosferatu","blocks":[{"text":"Nosferatu: A Symphony of Horror is a 1922 silent German Expressionist vampire film directed by F. W. Murnau from a screenplay by Henrik Galeen. It stars Max Schreck as Count Orlok, a vampire who preys on the wife of his estate agent and brings a plague to their town."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/90/Nosferatu_poster_%28Albin_Grau%2C_1922%29_1.jpg/330px-Nosferatu_poster_%28Albin_Grau%2C_1922%29_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nosferatu","wikidata":"Q151895"},{"title":"Nosferatu (2024 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Nosferatu is a 2024 American Gothic horror film written and directed by Robert Eggers. It is a remake of Nosferatu: A Symphony of Horror (1922), which was in turn inspired by Bram Stoker's novel Dracula (1897); the film combines elements of both. It stars Bill Skarsgård, Nicholas Hoult, Lily-Rose Depp, Aaron Taylor-Johnson, Emma Corrin, and Willem Dafoe."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/48/Nosferatu_IMAX_poster_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nosferatu_(2024_film)","wikidata":"Q116361132"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Max_Schreck_as_Count_Orlok_in_Nosferatu_%E2%80%93_Eine_Symphonie_des_Grauens_%281922%29.jpg/500px-Max_Schreck_as_Count_Orlok_in_Nosferatu_%E2%80%93_Eine_Symphonie_des_Grauens_%281922%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Max_Schreck_as_Count_Orlok_in_Nosferatu_%E2%80%93_Eine_Symphonie_des_Grauens_%28192